cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "USD-N: Deterministic USD Issuance with External BTC Constraint Modeling"

message: >
  If you use this software in research, simulations, audits, or policy analysis,
  please cite it using the metadata below.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Feeney
    given-names: Don Michael

repository-code: https://github.com/dfeen87/usd-n

url: https://github.com/dfeen87/usd-n

version: 4.1.0

date-released: 2026-02-08

license: MIT

abstract: >
  USD-N is a deterministic monetary simulation and policy modeling system that
  treats Bitcoin as an external, non-sovereign constraint rather than a pegged
  asset or issuance target. The system provides explicit reserve modeling,
  auditable invariants, and programmatic USD/BTC alignment metrics—including
  reserve coverage, BTC reserve share, and stress-adjusted issuance multipliers—
  to support simulations, governance analysis, and audit workflows without
  introducing custody, convertibility, or price coupling.
